'''''Lathyrus angulatus''''' is a species of [[Lathyrus|wild pea]] known by the common name '''angled pea'''.

It is native to southern Europe and North Africa, and it is known from elsewhere as an [[introduced species]].

This is an annual herb with a flanged, hairless stem. Each leaf is made up of two leaflike leaflets each a few centimeters long and very narrow. It has tiny coiling [[tendril]]s. The [[inflorescence]] holds a solitary flower on a long bristle-tipped [[peduncle (botany)|peduncle]] with the flower situated midway. The purple pea flower is about a centimeter wide. The fruit is a hairless [[Dehiscence (botany)|dehiscent]] legume pod.

